# Forms and user-generated content rules

## Reactive Forms

- **Use Reactive Forms** - always use `ReactiveFormsModule` and `FormBuilder`
- **Validation** - use built-in Angular validators (`Validators.required`, `Validators.email`)
- **Custom validators** - create custom validators only when necessary

Example:
```typescript
this.form = this.fb.group({
  name: ['', Validators.required],
  email: ['', [Validators.required, Validators.email]],
  phone: ['', Validators.required],
  resume: [null],
});
```

## Phone validation

- **libphonenumber-js** - use the `libphonenumber-js` library for phone validation and formatting
- **CountryService** - use `CountryService` to get country code and dial code
- **Formatting** - format the phone in international format before submission

Example:
```typescript
import { parsePhoneNumber, isValidPhoneNumber } from 'libphonenumber-js';

const selectedCountry = this.countryService.currentCountry;
const phoneNumber = this.form.get('phone')?.value || '';
const fullPhone = `${selectedCountry.dialCode}${phoneNumber}`;

if (!isValidPhoneNumber(fullPhone)) {
  this.phoneError = this.translationService.get('common_validation_phone');
  return;
}

const parsedPhone = parsePhoneNumber(fullPhone);
const formattedPhone = parsedPhone.formatInternational();
```

## Form components

- **Use existing components** - use components from `libs/ui/src/components/` (`@guru/ui`):
  - `InputTextComponent`
  - `InputEmailComponent`
  - `InputPhoneComponent`
  - `InputTextareaComponent`
  - `InputFileComponent`
  - `InputSelectComponent`
  - `SubmitButtonComponent`

- **Pass control** - pass `FormControl` via `[control]="form.get('fieldName')!"`

- **Use translations** - ALL `label` and `placeholder` MUST use translation keys via `{{ 'key' | translate }}`. See `205-frontend-i18n.mdc` for detailed rules

Example:
```html
<app-input-text
  [control]="form.get('fullName')!"
  id="fullName"
  label="{{ 'common_name' | translate }}"
  placeholder="{{ 'common_name_placeholder' | translate }}"
/>

<app-input-email
  [control]="form.get('email')!"
  id="email"
/>

<app-input-phone
  [control]="form.get('phone')!"
  id="phone"
  label="{{ 'common_phone_number' | translate }}"
  placeholder="{{ 'common_phone_placeholder' | translate }}"
  [phoneError]="phoneError"
/>
```

## Form submission handling

- **Check validity** - check `form.invalid` before submission
- **`markAllAsTouched()`** - call to display validation errors
- **Error handling** - handle submission errors and show messages to the user

Example:
```typescript
onSubmit(): void {
  if (this.form.invalid) {
    this.form.markAllAsTouched();
    return;
  }

  // Validation and submission
  this.isSubmitting = true;

  this.apiService.post$(endpoint, formData)
    .pipe(takeUntilDestroyed(this.destroyRef))
    .subscribe({
      next: (response) => {
        alert(this.translationService.get('common_resume_success'));
        this.form.reset();
        this.isSubmitting = false;
      },
      error: (error) => {
        alert(this.translationService.get('common_resume_error'));
        this.isSubmitting = false;
      },
    });
}
```

## File upload

- **FormData** - use `FormData` to send files
- **Size validation** - check file size before upload (if necessary)
- **File types** - check file type (if necessary)

Example:
```typescript
const formData = new FormData();
formData.append('Name', this.form.get('name')?.value);
formData.append('Email', this.form.get('email')?.value);

const resumeFile = this.form.get('resume')?.value;
if (resumeFile) {
  formData.append('Resume', resumeFile);
}

this.apiService.post$(endpoint, formData, {
  // File upload options
})
  .pipe(takeUntilDestroyed(this.destroyRef))
  .subscribe();
```

## Loading state

- **`isSubmitting`** - use a flag to track submission state
- **Disable form** - disable the form during submission via `[disabled]="isSubmitting"`

Example:
```html
<app-submit-button [isSubmitting]="isSubmitting" />
```

## User-generated content security

- **DomSanitizer** - use `DomSanitizer` to safely display HTML content
- **SafeHtml** - use the `SafeHtml` type for sanitized content

Example:
```typescript
import { DomSanitizer, SafeHtml } from '@angular/platform-browser';

constructor(
  private readonly sanitizer: DomSanitizer,
) {
}

getSafeHtml(content: string): SafeHtml {
  return this.sanitizer.sanitize(SecurityContext.HTML, content) || '';
}
```
